  "title": "Optimizer-Friendly Instrumentation for Event Quantification with PRUE Algorithm",
  "abstract": "Event quantification provides frequency information for runtime events and is widely used to build fast, secure, and reliable software and systems. It is usually achieved through instrumentation that introduces new instructions into programs but has significant runtime overhead. A key challenge in developing efficient instrumentation is that the instrumentation can barely benefit from modern compiler optimizations because the additional instructions introduce side effects that complicate the optimization process.",
